<title>CHINA: China province 1997 cotton output seen 440,000 T.</title>
<headline>China province 1997 cotton output seen 440,000 T.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's eastern Shandong province is expected to produce 440,000 tonnes of cotton in 1997, the China Economic Times said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The acreage under cotton has been boosted in recent years in the province because of falling grain prices, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Shandong province plans to plant 533,280 hectares with cotton crops in 1997, it said, but gave no further details.</p>
<p>China produced a total of 4.2 million tonnes of cotton in 1996, down by 11.7 percent compared with the previous year, official figures show.</p>
</text>
